        <h3 class="font-medium text-tk-ink">Why limit sessions at the same time, and not hours?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          Charging by the hour punishes people who work by hand. An account
          manager keeping 3 profiles open 8 hours a day would rack up 720 hours a month
          and a surprise bill. Instead, you pay for how many sessions you can
          run at the same time, and use them as much as you like within that
          limit. The optional AI agent has its own included monthly budget.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-medium text-tk-ink">Can I switch tiers mid-month?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          Yes. Moving up takes effect right away and you pay only the
          difference for the rest of the billing period. Moving down takes
          effect at your next renewal. New limits apply the next time you
          start a session.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-medium text-tk-ink">Does the free tier expire?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          No. The free tier never expires: one profile, one session at a
          time of up to 20 minutes, no card. Subscribe to a paid tier from
          your dashboard when you need more. That could be the API, every
          device type, or longer sessions. It could also be more profiles,
          more sessions at the same time, or the AI agent. Paid tiers also
          let sessions go out through your own VPN connection, not just a
          proxy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10">
      <a href="/faq/" class="btn-secondary">See full FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </Section>

